===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Able to be [[sustained]].
# Able to be produced or sustained for an [[indefinite]] [[period]] without [[damaging]] the [[environment]], or without [[depleting]] a [[resource]]; [[renewable]].
#: {{ux|en|'''sustainable''' economy}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Kate L. Harrison|title=The Green Bride Guide|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=O5FyqGQmdpUC&pg=PA174&dq=sustainable|page=174|isbn=140221345X
|passage=In addition to the resources listed in the organic and local food sections earlier, a good source of '''sustainable''' meat is Heritage Foods USA (heritagefoodsusa.com).}}
#* '''2008''' August–October, Dawn Brighid, "A Taste of Hope", in ''Organic Gardening'', ISSN 1536-108X, volume 55, number 6, page 73&nbsp;[http://books.google.com/books?id=S8MDAAAAMBAJ&pg=PA73&dq=%22that+sustainable%22]:
#*: Some critics have asserted that '''sustainable''' food is "elitist"; that it's too expensive and not widely available.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=w:Anthony Bourdain|title=w:Medium Raw|isbn=9780061718946|page=129|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=_-Z6Umuq68EC&pg=PA129&dq=sustainable
|passage=A city on a hill—or many cities on hills—surrounded by unbroken vistas of beautiful countryside; small, thriving, family-run farms growing organic, seasonal, and '''sustainable''' fruits and vegetables specific to the region.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2019|author=Jason Hickel|title=[https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2019/mar/05/climate-breakdown-uk-greener-new-deal-cap-consumption Climate breakdown is coming. The UK needs a Greener New Deal]|journal=Guardian.
|passage=Right now, rich nations devour 28 tonnes of material per person per year – including everything from fish to forests, plastics to metals. That’s four times more than ecologists say is '''sustainable'''.}}

